  "Question": "Let \\(A=\\{1,2\\}\\) and \\(B=\\{1,2,3\\}\\). If “\\(x\\in A\\)” implies “\\(x\\in B\\)”, record this implication as 1; if it does not, record it as 0. What should be recorded here?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(A\\) is a subset of \\(B\\), so if \\(x\\) belongs to \\(A\\), it must belong to \\(B\\). The implication holds, so record 1.",
